      "id": "https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/earth-wind-and-fire-fred-white-dead-obit-1234655162/",
      "title": "Earth, Wind and Fire Drumming Prodigy Fred White Dead at 67",
      "url": "https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/earth-wind-and-fire-fred-white-dead-obit-1234655162/",
      "publishedDate": "2023-01-02T20:05:32.000Z",
      "author": "Tessa Stuart",
      "text": "×\n\n[×](https://www.rollingstone.com/www.rollingstone.com)\n\n[Skip to main content](https://www.rollingstone.com/www.rollingstone.com#pagetop)\n\nBy\n[Tessa Stuart](https://www.rollingstone.com/author/tessa-stuart/)\n\n### [Tessa Stuart](https://www.rollingstone.com/author/tessa-stuart/)\n\n[Contact Tessa Stuart on X](https://twitter.com/tessastuart)\n\n[View all posts by Tessa Stuart](https://www.rollingstone.com/author/tessa-stuart/)\n\nJanuary 2, 2023\n\nEarth, Wind & Fire, Fred White,\nAhoy, Rotterdam, 14-3-1979,\nFoto Rob VerhorstRedferns\n\nFred White, drummer for the groundbreaking funk outfit [Earth, Wind and Fire](https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-lists/earth-wind-fire-12-essential-songs-26670/sweetbacks-theme-1971-27970/) — and half-brother of lead singer Maurice and brother of bassist Verdine White — has died, his family announced on Jan. 1. White was 67 years old.\n\n“He joins our brothers Maurice, Monte, and Ronald in heaven and is now drumming with the angels,” Verdine White wrote in a tribute shared on Instagram. (He did not disclose a cause of death; [Maurice White died after a battle with Parkinson’s Disease](https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/maurice-white-earth-wind-fire-singer-and-co-founder-dead-at-74-99968/) in 2016.)\n\n> [View this post on Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/p/Cm5Qo0npjH1/?utm_source=ig_embed&utm_campaign=loading)\n>\n> [A post shared by Verdine White (@verdine\\_white)](https://www.instagram.com/p/Cm5Qo0npjH1/?utm_source=ig_embed&utm_campaign=loading)\n\nA child prodigy who began drumming at age nine before going on to earn his first gold record at the age of 16 for his work on Donny Hathaway’s _Live_ — which made _Rolling Stone_’s list of [50 greatest live albums of all time](https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-lists/50-greatest-live-albums-of-all-time-173246/little-feat-waiting-for-columbus-1978-153332/) — White joined his brothers’ band in 1974 just before the group shot to stardom on the success of its sixth studio album, _That’s the Way of the World_. Both the album and the single, “Shining Star,” hit number 1 on the Billboard charts.\n\nEarth, Wind and Fire went on to sell more than 90 million records, cementing its status as one of the best-selling bands of all time. Beloved by critics as well as fans, the band was nominated for 17 Grammys, and won six.\n\nMore than two dozen members have cycled in and out of Earth, Wind and Fire since its founding in 1969, but White was part of the nine-man lineup [inducted into the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame](https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/earth-wind-and-fire-groove-into-hall-243278/) in 2000.\n\n## Trending Stories\n\n[**Taylor Swift Unveils ‘The Life of a Showgirl’ Cover, Sabrina Carpenter Feature**](https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/taylor-swift-life-of-showgirl-details-cover-new-heights-1235406130/)[**Trump Privately Dismissed Epstein Victims as ‘Democrats’**](https://www.rollingstone.com/politics/politics-features/trump-privately-dismissed-eps",
      "favicon": "https://www.rollingstone.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/R-Avatar_512x512_flat.png?w=32"
    },
    {
      "id": "https://www.npr.org/2023/01/02/1146587565/fred-white-drummer-earth-wind-fire-dead",
      "title": "Fred White, drummer for the band Earth, Wind & Fire, has died - NPR",
      "url": "https://www.npr.org/2023/01/02/1146587565/fred-white-drummer-earth-wind-fire-dead",
      "publishedDate": "2023-01-02T00:00:00.000Z",
      "author": "Becky Sullivan",
      "text": "Accessibility links\n\n- [Skip to main content](https://www.npr.org/www.npr.org#mainContent)\n- [Keyboard shortcuts for audio player](https://help.npr.org/contact/s/article?name=what-are-the-keyboard-shortcuts-for-using-the-npr-org-audio-player)\n\n**Fred White, drummer for the band Earth, Wind & Fire, has died** **White, the younger brother of the band's founder and principal songwriter Maurice White, joined the group in the mid-1970s and went on to lay the backbone for hits like \"September\" and \"Shining Star.\"**\n\n### [Obituaries](https://www.npr.org/sections/obituaries/)\n\n# Fred White, drummer for the band Earth, Wind & Fire, has died\n\nJanuary 2, 20235:13 PM ET\n\n[Becky Sullivan](https://www.npr.org/people/348743421/becky-sullivan)\n\nFred White, who played drums for the era-defining and genre-defying band Earth, Wind & Fire, has died at the age of 67, his brother and the band announced on social media.\n\n\"Our family is saddened today with the loss of an amazing and talented family member, our beloved brother Frederick Eugene 'Freddie' White,\" wrote his brother and bandmate [Verdine White on Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/p/Cm5Qo0npjH1/) on Sunday. No cause of death has yet been released.\n\n> [View this post on Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/p/Cm5Qo0npjH1/?utm_source=ig_embed&utm_campaign=loading)\n>\n> [A post shared by Verdine White(@verdine\\_white)](https://www.instagram.com/p/Cm5Qo0npjH1/?utm_source=ig_embed&utm_campaign=loading)\n\nFred White was born in 1955 in Chicago into a family of musicians, including older brothers Verdine and Maurice White. He showed talent at the drums early in life — a \"child protégé,\" his brother Verdine said — and even as a teenager found success playing drums in Chicago for acts including Donny Hathaway.\n\n\"At home and beyond he was the wonderful bro that was always entertaining and delightfully mischievous,\" his brother wrote. \"We could always count on him to make a seemingly bad situation more light hearted.\"\n\nIn 1970, Maurice moved to Los Angeles and founded Earth, Wind & Fire, and Verdine joined a few months later.\n\nA few years later, they coaxed their younger brother to join the group as a primary drummer.\n\n### [The Record](https://www.npr.org/sections/therecord/)\n\n### [Maurice White: The Audacity Of Uplift](https://www.npr.org/sections/therecord/2016/02/05/465703176/maurice-white-the-audacity-of-uplift)\n\nFred White went on to play the drums for the funk-soul-disco-R&B-fusion band in its heyday through the mid-1980s, including on all six albums in Earth, Wind & Fire's remarkable run of consecutive top 10 records on the Billboard pop chart.\n\nHis tight and energetic beats made up the backbone of hits like \"Shining Star,\" \"Let's Groove\" and – of course – the enduring mega-hit \"September,\" which hit No. 8 on the _Billboard_ Hot 100 when it was released and has nearly 1.2 billion streams on Spotify.\n\n> [View this post on Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/reel/Cm43heioWlH/?utm_source=ig_embed&utm_campaign=loadi",
      "favicon": "https://media.npr.org/chrome/favicon/favicon-32x32.png"
    },
